ci you want to keep.</div><div><br></div><div>Hope that helps,</div><div>Zhian</div><div><br></div><div>On Friday, January 1, 2016 at 10:12:18 AM UTC-8, Jennifer Gruhn wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello!  <br><br>I created a gencone object by importing a genalex-structured file.  I have 2937 SNPs across 42 individuals, comprising 6 populations.  (I treat the SNPs as microsatellite loci in the file, so that 1-4 below represents either A, C, G, or T.):<div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2937</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">42</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br> <br> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Ind</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Pop</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Crater</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Crater</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><